\subsection{Continuous magnetic hard-iron correction}
\label{sec:mag-hard-iron}
\label{sec:mag-gauge}
Startup averaging cannot separate a body-fixed offset from the field at a
single attitude. With yaw-stripped body-to-level proxy rotation $\mat A_i$,
level field $\vct B_\ell$, and additive offset $\vct b_m$,
\begin{equation}
\vct m_i=\mat A_i^{\top}\vct B_\ell+\vct b_m+\vct n_i .
\label{eq:mag-offset-model}
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\bar{\vct w}
=\frac{1}{N}\sum_i\mat A_i\vct m_i
=\vct B_\ell+\bar{\mat A}\vct b_m,
\qquad
\bar{\mat A}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_i\mat A_i .
\label{eq:mag-ref-average}
\end{equation}
Eliminating the unknown field gives
\begin{equation}
\underbrace{(\mat I-\bar{\mat A}^{\top}\bar{\mat A})}_{\mat M}\vct b_m
=\bar{\vct m}-\bar{\mat A}^{\top}\bar{\vct w} .
\label{eq:mag-normal}
\end{equation}
Small roll/pitch motion supplies information but leaves weakly excited
components poorly conditioned.

\label{sec:mag-hi-estimator}
An exponentially weighted fit with \SI{600}{s} memory uses raw magnetometer samples and
the independent proxy rotations, updating once per second. The regularized
solve is
\begin{equation}
\left[\mat M+\left(\rho_0+\rho_1\frac{\operatorname{tr}\mat M}{3}\right)
\mat I\right]\hat{\vct b}_m
=\bar{\vct m}-\bar{\mat A}^{\top}\bar{\vct w},
\label{eq:mag-ridge}
\end{equation}
with fixed $\rho_0=5\times10^{-4}$ and $\rho_1=0.25$.
Acceptance requires at least 500 effective samples,
$N\lambda_{\min}(\mat M)\ge2$, offset norm below 35\% of the field, and
level-frame residual at most \SI{3}{\micro\tesla} RMS.
The ridge limits both ill-conditioning and distortion aliased into the
additive model; its absolute floor is not inferred from the information gate.

\label{sec:mag-hi-apply}
Accepted offsets are subtracted from the raw stream with a \SI{45}{s} time
constant. The learned reference retains its horizontal direction while its
magnitude and dip adjust, allowing ordinary magnetic corrections to remove
yaw bias without an attitude or covariance reset. Without an accepted fit,
measurement and reference remain unchanged.

\label{sec:mag-hi-limits}
Fixed-heading data cannot generally identify soft iron or sensor misalignment.
Those terms may pass the additive residual gate and can degrade correction;
Sec.~\ref{sec:mag-hi-results} reports the evaluated draw.
